= Introduction
The CLEC Project aims to enhance the digital capabilities of educators through targeted training programs. This impact assessment report evaluates the upcoming "Digital Literacy & AI Integration Workshop", a 2-credit course scheduled from November 1, 2026, to November 5, 2026. The initiative is designed to address the growing need for advanced technological integration in educational institutions.

= Objectives
- To assess the participation demographics for the Digital Literacy & AI Integration Workshop.
- To provide a geographical overview of the participating institutions.
- To quantify the expected impact of the training on the educational ecosystem across various districts.

= Methodology
This report is based on the registration data for the workshop. Quantitative analysis was performed on the participant database, evaluating the spread of participants across schools and regions. The dataset includes participant names, school affiliations, and contact information strictly sourced from the project database.

= Geographical Overview
The participants for the upcoming workshop represent a diverse geographical spread, indicating a wide-reaching impact of the CLEC Project. 

